emeter","function":"measure","score":0.5181,"evidence":"de; in; in de","documented_marker":false,"photo":null}],"markers":{"total":54,"by_label":{"asbestos_positive":28,"not_sampled":18,"sampled_negative":8},"never_sampled":18,"codes":["V07773","V10565","V12094.1","V12094.2","V12094.3","V15320.b","V21022","V21491","V21647.2","V21647.3","V21848","V21980.2","V25603.b","V27609","V27647","V32340.1","V32358","V35401"],"note":"The museum's own catalogue material field says \"Gevaarlijke stoffen / Hazardous substance\" on these objects. That is documentation, not a prediction, and it was kept out of every feature so no model can restate the label. Objects the museum itself marks hazardous and never sampled are the first candidates for a sample."},"location":{"template":"data/processed/boerhaave/asbestos_location_template.csv","script":"scripts/analysis/asbestos_locations.py","rows":438,"coded":0,"ready":false},"caveats":["Only 131 of 483 inspection lines were sampled (42 objects positive, 46 sampled negative, 348 never sampled). The museum chose what to test; absolute rates are not collection prevalence.","A never-sampled object is unknown, never negative.","The hazard is a component (gasket, cord, board, cable sheath, felt), not the whole object; a negative sample does not clear the object.","The museum's own catalogue material field says \"Gevaarlijke stoffen / Hazardous substance\" on 54 objects. That documented marker is reported separately and is not a model feature, so no model can restate the label.","n = 88 labelled objects cannot support a claim about asbestos content. These models are decision support for choosing what to sample next, not a safety clearance.","The image/text probes rest on the 18 labelled objects that have a frozen T-029 vector: a demonstration of the pipeline, not evidence."],"power_statement":"n = 88 labelled objects (42 positive, 46 negative) over 16 function classes. A text model has hundreds of candidate terms, so events per variable are far below 1; the cross-validated numbers below cannot support a claim about which objects contain asbestos. They can order the next samples for a curator.","selection_bias":"The museum sampled the objects it judged suspect, so the positive share among sampled objects is an upper bound on nothing: it is a sampling artefact, not prevalence."}